'''Eureka Forbes Limited''' is an Indian home appliances company based in [[Mumbai]]. It makes [[water purification]] devices, vacuum cleaners, air purification systems, and home security products.<ref>{{cite news |title=SP Group looks at listing or stake-sale of Eureka Forbes |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/sp-group-looks-at-listing-or-stake-sale-of-eureka-forbes/articleshow/72133838.cms |access-date=17 February 2023 |work=The Times of India |date=20 November 2019}}</ref>

==History==
Eureka Forbes was founded on 15th February 1982 as a 60:40 joint venture between [[Tata Group]]'s [[Forbes (engineering company)|Forbes & Company]] and Swedish manufacturer [[Electrolux]]. In 2001, Tata Group sold Forbes & Company to [[Shapoorji Pallonji Group]] and, four years later, Electrolux sold its 40% stake in Eureka Forbes to Forbes & Company.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Coster |first1=Helen |title=Every Salesman a King |url=https://www.forbes.com/global/2005/1003/018A.html |access-date=17 February 2023 |work=Forbes |language=en}}</ref>

In 2010, Eureka Forbes acquired a 25% stake in Swiss consumer products company Lux International. In 2013, Eureka Forbes increased its stake to become the controlling shareholder in Lux International.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mitra |first1=Sounak |title=Eureka Forbes to acquire majority stake in Lux International |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/eureka-forbes-to-acquire-majority-stake-in-lux-international-113051500892_1.html |access-date=17 February 2023 |work=Business Standard India |date=15 May 2013}}</ref>

In 2022, [[Advent International]] bought out [[Shapoorji Pallonji Group]]'s entire stake in Eureka Forbes, after Eureka Forbes was separated from Forbes & Company and listed on the [[Bombay Stock Exchange|BSE]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Shapoorji Pallonji and Co exits from Eureka Forbes |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/company/corporate-trends/shapoorji-pallonji-and-co-exits-from-eureka-forbes/articleshow/92877877.cms |access-date=17 February 2023 |work=The Economic Times |date=14 July 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=PE major Advent International buys majority stake in Eureka Forbes |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/advent-acquires-eureka-forbes-at-an-enterprise-valuation-of-rs-4-400-crore-121091900814_1.html |access-date=1 October 2021 |work=Business Standard}}</ref>

